# Title: Xwizard.EXE Execution From Non-Default Location
# ID: 193d5ccd-6f59-40c6-b5b0-8e32d5ddd3d1
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2021-09-20
# Tags: attack.privilege-escalation, attack.persistence, attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1574.001
# Description: Detects the execution of Xwizard tool from a non-default directory.
# When executed from a non-default directory, this utility can be abused in order to side load a custom version of "xwizards.dll".
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.executable:*\\xwizard.exe) OR (process.pe.original_file_name:"xwizard.exe")) AND NOT (((process.executable:C:\\Windows\\System32\\* OR process.executable:C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\* OR process.executable:C:\\Windows\\WinSxS\\*))))
